<h3>Bottlenecks / follow-ups</h3>
<ol>
<li>Gallery JPEGs can still be tightened (~99 KiB potential savings in earlier lab checks)  </li>
<li>Deferred GTM can still affect INP after interaction — keep it deferred  </li>
<li>Maps iframes — keep <code>loading="lazy"</code>  </li>
<li>Pull field CWV from Search Console once CrUX data appears  </li>
</ol>
<p><b>Target:</b> keep field LCP p75 under 2.5 s; homepage stays in the green on PSI.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>HTTPS / TLS</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Control</th><th>Status</th></tr>
<tr><td>HTTPS</td><td>Enforced by Vercel</td></tr>
<tr><td>Certificate</td><td>Let's Encrypt, <code>www.regainhopedetox.com</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Expiry observed</td><td>~Sep 24, 2026 (auto-renew expected)</td></tr>
<tr><td>HSTS</td><td><code>max-age=63072000</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Mixed content</td><td>None detected</td></tr>
</table>
<hr/>
<h2>Action plan</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Priority</th><th>Action</th><th>Owner</th></tr>
<tr><td>P0</td><td>Rotate CTM key; move submit to Vercel serverless</td><td>Eng + CTM ops</td></tr>
<tr><td>P0</td><td>Remove <code>method="get"</code> / keep PII out of query strings</td><td>Eng</td></tr>
<tr><td>P0</td><td>Add security headers in <code>vercel.json</code></td><td>Eng</td></tr>
<tr><td>P1</td><td>Revisit form fields (Policy ID) + confirm CTM BAA</td><td>Legal + Eng</td></tr>
<tr><td>P1</td><td>Anti-spam + real submit error handling</td><td>Eng</td></tr>
<tr><td>P1</td><td><code>npm audit fix</code> + Astro upgrade plan</td><td>Eng</td></tr>
<tr><td>P1</td><td>Vercel dashboard hardening checklist</td><td>Ops</td></tr>
<tr><td>P2</td><td>Optimize gallery images</td><td>Eng</td></tr>
<tr><td>P2</td><td>CSP report-only → enforce</td><td>Eng</td></tr>
<tr><td>P2</td><td>Replace starter README with real project docs</td><td>Eng</td></tr>
<tr><td>P2</td><td>Capture field CWV (CrUX / Search Console)</td><td>Eng</td></tr>
<tr><td>P3</td><td>Accessibility heading/label fixes</td><td>Eng</td></tr>
</table>
<hr/>
<h2>Conclusion</h2>
<p>Performance and Astro architecture are in excellent shape (PSI Mobile 97 / Desktop 100). What's blocking a clean "production-ready / template for other AI sites" sign-off is security engineering: client-side lead credentials, insurance-data handling, and Vercel header hardening.</p>
<p>Closing P0 and P1 is enough to treat this stack as the baseline for similar Hopewell AI client sites.</p>
<hr/>
<p><i>Secrets are redacted in this report. Rotate any FormReactor key that has appeared in the repo or public HTML.</i></p>
